# Code Indexer MCP Server

Use the `code-indexer` MCP server to search code semantically before making changes.

## Tools
- `code_search(project_name, query, limit)` - Search code with natural language
- `code_index(project_name, root_path, include_paths, extensions, force)` - Index a project
- `code_status(project_name?)` - Check status (omit project_name to list all)
- `watch_project(project_name)` - Auto re-index on file changes
- `unwatch_project(project_name)` - Stop watching
- `list_watched()` - List watched projects
- `delete_project(project_name)` - Remove project index

## When to Search
- Before editing: find related code and existing patterns
- When user asks "where is X?" or "how does Y work?"
- To find usage examples of functions/types

## Indexed Projects
- `lapp-backend` - Rust backend at `./backend` (src/, .rs files)
- `lapp-frontend` - Next.js frontend at `./Pyckx-frontend` (app/, components/, lib/, .ts/.tsx files)

## Usage Examples

### Search for code
```json
{"project_name": "lapp-backend", "query": "authentication handler", "limit": 5}
```

### Index a project (first time only)
```json
{"project_name": "lapp-backend", "root_path": "./backend", "include_paths": ["src"], "extensions": [".rs"]}
```

### Start watching for auto re-indexing
```json
{"project_name": "lapp-backend"}
```

## Tips
- Use descriptive queries: "error handling in login" > "error"
- Check `code_status` if search returns nothing
- Focus on results with score > 0.4
- Index must be done before searching a new project
- Use `watch_project` for active coding sessions
